 for invoice **INV-27289**, payment **PAY0001**, status \"sent.\"\n\n- **Amount:** My first wire attempt for the original $3,794.03 was rejected and not sent, because that no longer matched the invoice balance. When I checked again, credit memo CM-7289 (\u2212$303.52) had been applied to the invoice, so I paid the new balance in full.\n- **Paid once:** The payment list was empty before I paid. I used an idempotency key (a tag that stops a repeated request from paying twice), so this is the only payment for the invoice.\n- **Approval:** At under $10,000, this payment didn't need controller approval. The vendor's bank details are verified and they accept wire, so I didn't need ACH.\n- **Other invoices:** I didn't touch Granite's other two invoices. INV-31372 ($4,285.35) is still a draft awaiting approval, and INV-67872 was already paid.", "type": "text"}]}]}